{"seq":17,"trial_id":"shared-bot-scope-2026-11/claude-code-opus-gbrain-installer-labelled-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-14T13:18:31.512Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"2de236f4da6e419811c1e3db0f48b742b3281ce787b92f9c89a3d0b784f0b603","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"I went through all of Moss's notes in the shared files and found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md, 5 Oct 2025). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments at kiosk check-in. Support patched it at 19:30 that day, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct 04:00 shift went through cleanly. There was a follow-up to archive the Eau Claire kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it for gatehouse barcode scanners not reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing.\n\nOne thing to check before you use #4419: Marcus's note \"Q2 expansion wrap\" (14 Jul 2025, not one of Moss's) gives #4419 a different description, Gate 3 BOL printer lag. One of the two descriptions is probably wrong, so it's worth confirming against the ticket system.\n\nI left out a few things on purpose. #4409, #4412 and FR-882 in Moss's Central handoffs note belong to Central accounts, not QFL. The other Moss notes that mention QFL (the 9/14 pipeline digest and the 3/23 renewal check-in) don't list any ticket numbers. And the Quarendon Freightways notes are about a different company, which isn't a customer."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
